// suggested_command is a validated argv ARRAY. We hand its
// elements to nettools re-checked at run time, but we must NOT
// shell-join them (that re-opens the quoting surface event_routing's
// own docstring warns against). The Code node below builds argv for
// an HTTP/SSH executor that takes an array, or you invoke your own
// nettools wrapper that accepts JSON argv on stdin. See
// examples/systemd/nettools-webhook.py for the argv-list pattern.
const d = JSON.parse($json.stdout).decisions.find(x => x.routable);
return [{ json: { argv: d.suggested_command } }];
